  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read proxy.dispatch_commitment and proxy.pdp_decision_relation. The posture release is unchanged: authorization/capability.rs was restructured (136 lines, the capability's internals and argument grouping), and request_stages.rs and dispatch_obligations.rs changed in what the dispatched exchange still owes after dispatch, not in how the body is released. scripts/authorization_provenance_gate.py, whose clauses 4, 7 and 10 are the claim's structural half, passes on the current tree: the authority reads its action from the signed body, builds postures in one operation, and the dispatch consumes a body only a decision can release. The claim, premises and dependencies are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane was not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor, and every tested symbol the unit names still names a test function.",
